R"VG(
# medieval.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the annal (a year on a tablet or a scroll), the chronicle (several years in a codex; an
# industrial codex and a late age's crystal keep it too), the decree (the rule's law). The events are the annal register's (annal*.vg);
# what the scribe adds is here: the quiet years in the people's own goods, the chronicler's preface and asides (the year's own facts:
# its harvest, its war, its sickness), the decree's reasons (a law the history made: `@event law med.dec`) and its clauses.

@root med.chr.*

# ---- the annal: one year's entries, terse -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.annal (words=6..76)
  (tense=past 2) {annal.head} {@entries annal 3}
  (tense=past) {annal.head} {@entries annal 2} {med.ann.note}

annal.head (formula)
  (reign>0 has:$ruler) Year {#year:digits} of {city}, the {#reign:ord} year of {$ruler:poss} rule.
  Year {#year:digits} of {city}.
  The {#year:ord} year from the founding of {city}.
  (reign>0 has:$ruler) In the {#reign:ord} year of {$ruler:full}.
  (reign>0 has:$ruler.epithet) In the {#reign:ord} year of {$ruler:full} {$ruler.epithet}.
  Year {#year:digits}, in {era}.
  At {$home}, the year {#year:digits}.
  (gov=council|gov=republic|gov=assembly) Year {#year:digits}, {ruler.the} sitting at {$seat}.
  (gov=theocracy) Year {#year:digits} of {city}, in the keeping of {holyplace}.
  (moons>0) Year {#year:digits}, counted by {moon}.

# a quiet year (the register's: `@entries` finds nothing)
annal.quiet (share=0.5)
  Nothing of note.
  A quiet year.
  A quiet year. The {crop} came in {med.ann.how}.
  Nothing of note, except that {annal.small}.
  Nothing was written this year but the count of the {vessel} in the stores.
  The year passed with nothing in it but the {crop} and the {herd}.
  Nothing happened worth the ink, except that {annal.small}.
  A year of {weather} and small quarrels, and nothing else to set down.
  The scribe has nothing to write but that the {fruit} were sweet.
  No war, no sickness, no stranger at the gate of {$home}; the {crop} came in {med.ann.how}.
  Quiet. The {herd} were counted twice and came out the same both times.
  Nothing, unless you count that {annal.small}.
  A year like the one before at {$home}, {crop} and {herd} and {weather}.
  (moons>0) A year of quiet. {moon} kept its time and so did we.
  (contact=1) Nothing of note, except that traders of the {other} came to {city2} with {trade}.
  The {craft} of {$home} sold well, and nothing else happened.
  No news at {$home} but the {bird} and {weather}.
  The {med.chr.trades} complained, the {herd} grew fat, and the year ended.

# the small things of a quiet year (a clause)
annal.small (share=0.6)
  the bell of {hall} cracked in the cold and was recast
  a {beast} with two heads was born at {city2} and shown at {festival}
  the roof of the granary was mended with {material}
  (moons>0) {moon} was red for a night
  the old {tree.n} by the gate came down in {weather}
  a fish was taken from {river} as long as a boat
  the {bird} came early and stayed late
  the {craft} of {city2} was sent for from the far towns
  a boy of {$home} walked to {mountain} and back for a wager
  the {herd} of {$seat} got into the {crop2} and ate it to the ground
  someone painted {motif.over} on the gate of {hall} and nobody would say who
  the price of {crop} fell so low that the farmers would not sell it
  the custom of {feast.custom} was kept with more noise than usual
  a whole cask of {drink} was spilt in the square at {festival}
  the oldest woman in {$home} died at a great age, and everyone went
  {fish} came up {river} so thick that they were taken by hand
  a well-digger at {city2} found old pots, and the priests took them away
  (comet=1) the hairy star was looked for and did not come
  (aurora=1) the lights in the north were seen as far south as {city2}
  (coast=1) a whale came ashore below {$seat}, and the town ate well
  (desert=1) it rained for a whole day, and the children were afraid of it

med.ann.how
  heavy
  late
  early
  thin but sound
  better than anyone had said
  wet
  as usual

# a note at a year's end (the annal's own, rare)
med.ann.note (share=0.4)
  The {crop} was {med.ann.how} that year.
  {time.of} the bells were rung for the {crop}.
  The roads were bad and the {herd} thin.
  Prices were high in the market at {$seat}, for {crop2} above all.
  The {fruit} failed, but nobody died of that.
  (harvest>=3) The granaries of {$home} were full of {crop} for once.
  The {med.chr.trades} of {$home} were busy all that year.
  The {pest} were in the {crop2}, and the cats were fat.
  A {bird.one} nested in the bell tower, and the bell was not rung until it flew.
  The {watersrc.n} ran low in {season.now}, and was cleaned.

# ---- the chronicle: several years, each a paragraph (`@years` tells each by `chronicle.year`, the empty runs by its `.gap`) ----

@root chronicle.year chronicle.year.gap

genre.chronicle (words=15..440)
  (tense=past age<=industrial) {chronicle.open} {@years 4 chronicle.year} {chronicle.close}
  (tense=past age<=industrial) {@years 5 chronicle.year}
  (tense=past 0.6 age<=industrial) {chronicle.open} {@years 7 chronicle.year} {chronicle.close}
  (tense=past 1.2 age<=industrial) {chronicle.open} {med.chr.preface}\n{@years 4 chronicle.year} {chronicle.close}
  (tense=past age>=futuristic) {chronicle.open} {med.chr.late}\n{@years 6 chronicle.year}\n{med.chr.late.end} {chronicle.close}
  (tense=past age>=futuristic) {chronicle.open} {@years 7 chronicle.year}\n{med.chr.late.end}

chronicle.open (formula)
  Here are written the years of {city}, as they were told to me.
  The chronicle of {city}, continued.
  (has:$seat) What follows is the record kept at {$seat}.
  In the name of {god}, the years.
  The years of {city}, set down at {holyplace}.
  (has:$ruler) The years of {city} to the rule of {$ruler:full}.
  Of the years of {city}, the next part.
  (age>=futuristic) The chronicle of {city}, kept as it was kept, year by year.

chronicle.close (formula)
  (2)
  Here ends this part of the chronicle.
  So far the years. The rest is for the next hand.
  Here the scribe rested.
  The rest is on the next roll.
  (age>=futuristic) The record continues.

# the chronicler on their sources, their task, their hand (a sentence or two before the years)
med.chr.preface (share=0.4)
  I had the earlier years from the old roll at {holyplace}, which the {pest} have been at.
  What I did not see I had from the old ones of {$home}, and I have written it as they said it, though they did not agree.
  The ink is made from {med.ink} and will last longer than I will.
  I write in the cold room over the {craft}-house at {$home}, and my hand is not what it was.
  Where the old roll and the old ones disagree about the {crop} years, I have followed the old ones, who ate them.
  The years before these are in another hand, a better one, and on {med.chr.on}.
  I have left out the quarrels of {$home} about the {med.chr.quarrel.s}; there were too many to write.
  I was told to write the years plainly by {ruler.the}, and I have tried.
  Some of these years I remember; the rest I have from {med.chr.source}.
  (age>=industrial) These years are copied from the old rolls of {holyplace}, word for word, and the spelling mended.
  (age>=futuristic) These years were kept on rolls first, then on {material}, then here. Nothing was changed but the hand.
  (value=learning) The years are written so that the young of {$home} may count them, and learn that the bad ones end.
  (value=piety) The years are written so that {god} may read them, though {god} saw them first.
  I am the {nth} to keep this chronicle at {$home}, and the first to complain about writing on {med.chr.on}.
  My teacher kept these years before me, with a {bird.one} feather and a temper.

med.chr.on
  vellum
  bark
  reed sheets
  {colour.any} cloth
  the back of old accounts

med.ink
  oak gall and rust
  soot and gum
  the black of {tree} bark
  burnt {crop} and water
  {crop2} ash and vinegar

med.chr.source
  the roll at {holyplace}
  the old women of {$home}
  the stones by {town.edge}
  my teacher, who had them from hers
  the songs, which are wrong about the numbers and right about everything else

chronicle.year
  (3) {chronicle.head} {@entries annal 3}
  (2) {chronicle.head} {@entries annal 4}
  (2) {chronicle.head} {@entries annal 3} {med.chr.aside}
  {chronicle.head} {med.chr.weather} {@entries annal 3}
chronicle.year.gap (formula)
  (gap>=2) Nothing of note in the years {#y0:digits} to {#y1:digits}.
  (gap>=2) The years {#y0:digits} to {#y1:digits} passed without anything worth the writing.
  (gap>=3 gap<=12) {#gap|quiet year}, and nothing in them but the harvests.
  (gap>12) Then {#gap} years of quiet, with nothing in them but the harvests.
  (gap=1) In {#y0:digits}, nothing of note.
  (gap=1) The year {#y0:digits} was quiet.
  (gap>=2) From {#y0:digits} to {#y1:digits} the years were quiet ones.
  (gap>=2) Of the years {#y0:digits} to {#y1:digits} nothing is written.

chronicle.head (formula)
  (3 gov=monarchy has:$ruler) Year {#y:digits} of {city}, the {#reign:ord} of {$ruler:poss} reign.
  (gov=monarchy has:$ruler) In the {#y:ord} year of {city}, {$ruler:full} holding the throne.
  (gov=monarchy has:$ruler.epithet) In the {#y:ord} year of {city}, {$ruler:full} {$ruler.epithet} on the throne.
  (gov=chiefs has:$ruler) Year {#y:digits}, {$ruler:full} at {$seat}.
  (gov=council|gov=republic|gov=assembly) Year {#y:digits} of {city}, under {ruler.the}.
  (gov=theocracy) Year {#y:digits} of {city}, in the keeping of the priests.
  (2) Year {#y:digits}.
  The {#y:ord} year from the founding.
  In the year {#y:digits}.

# the chronicler's own word on a year: its weather, its prices, its mood (the year's facts: harvest, war, sickness, famine, the stage)
med.chr.weather (share=0.35)
  (seasons=4) It was a year of {weather} early and {weather} late.
  The year began in {weather}, and the {herd} were kept in.
  The year began badly for the {crop} and mended for the {fruit}.
  (harvest<=1) A hungry year from the first; the {crop} was eaten green.
  (harvest>=3) A fat year from the first; the {vessel} could not hold it.
  The year came in with {weather} and went out with {weather}.
  It was the year the {bird} came early to {$home}.
  It was a year for the {craft} and a bad one for the {crop}.
  The year was {med.chr.adj}, and the {herd} were {med.chr.herdwere}.
  In that year the {fruit} were {med.chr.fruitwere}.
  That year the {crop} was {med.chr.cropwas} and the {crop2} was {med.chr.cropwas}.
  That year {season.any} came {med.chr.came} to {$home}, and is remembered for it.
  It was a {med.chr.adj} year at {$home}, and a {med.chr.adj} one at {city2}.

med.chr.came
  late
  early
  hard
  gently
  twice

med.chr.herdwere
  thin
  fat
  few
  sick
  restless

med.chr.fruitwere
  small and sweet
  many and sour
  late
  eaten by the {bird}

med.chr.cropwas
  late
  early
  thin
  heavy
  good
  middling

med.chr.adj
  long
  short
  cold
  wet
  dry
  loud
  quiet
  hard
  kind

med.chr.poor
  {crop2} and bark
  {veg} and little else
  the {herd} they should have kept
  acorns, the way the old ones did
  bread made with sawdust

med.chr.trades
  weavers
  potters
  smiths
  carters
  boatmen
  dyers

med.chr.quarrel
  the boundary of the {crop} fields above {$home}
  who should ring the bell at {holyplace}
  the weights of the market at {$seat}
  the {watersrc.n} and who might draw from it
  a {beast} that nobody would own
  the order of the houses in the procession at {festival}

med.chr.said
  had gone grey in a night
  would not eat {food}
  had taken a fancy to the {craft}
  wept at {festival}
  could not read, and did not need to

med.unit
  {med.unit.w}
med.unit.w (people=2)
  measure
  basket
  sack
  load
  handful

)VG"
